# Database Rules

## Migrations

- Location: `database/migrations/`
- Use `foreignId()->constrained()` for relations (`bus_id`, `route_id`, `driver_id`).
- Index foreign keys and frequently filtered columns (status, `created_at` on logs).

## Models

- Explicit `$fillable` and `casts()` (see `User` model).
- Define relationships with return types.
- Use eager loading to prevent N+1 on fleet dashboards.

## Domain tables (existing)

`routes`, `stops`, `buses`, `drivers`, `trips`, `gps_logs`, `dispatch_logs`, `schedules`, `service_alerts`, `incidents`, `maintenance_records`, `demand_*`, `commuter_trips`, `users`.

## Seeders

- `database/seeders/UserSeeder.php` for role-based test users.
- Keep seeders safe for local/dev; no production secrets.

## Do not

- Change schema without a new migration.
- Drop columns in use without checking models and views.
- Query from Blade — load in controller/service.

## Commands

`php artisan migrate`, `php artisan migrate:status`, `php artisan db:seed`
